<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 110,478 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 110,478 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 110,478 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 71,759 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	October 27</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 9,448	 7,271</p>
<p>    Import cargo	     101,030	64,488</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, five were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Jet oil		  25,000	 Chilham Castle     29/10</p>
<p>High speed diesel    52,000	 Al-Maqwa	     31/10</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     30,060	 Pan Queen	    29/10</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     25,345	 Sea Harmony	  29/10</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
